- YouTube: 1920x1080, 16:9.
- YouTube Shorts: 1080x1920, 9:16.
- Instagram Reels: 1080x1920, 9:16.
- Instagram Square: 1080x1080, 1:1.
- Facebook Landscape: 1920x1080, 16:9.
- Custom width, height and frame rate.
5. Text, Captions and Audio
- Add editable titles and text overlays.
- Import and edit SRT subtitle files.
- Provide manual subtitle creation and timing controls.
- Add background music and voice-over tracks.
- Provide audio trimming, volume adjustment and fade-in/fade-out.
- Add Kannada and English fonts where supported.
- Include optional AI-assisted scripts, captions and voice-over using configured APIs.
- Never claim that automatic speech recognition or AI generation works unless the required engine or API is connected.
6. AI Creator Tools
Create separate tools for:
- Script-to-video planning.
- Scene and storyboard generation.
- AI image and video generation integrations.
- Automatic caption generation.
- Video title and description suggestions.
- Hashtag suggestions.
- Thumbnail creation with editable text, images and layouts.
Clearly distinguish working local features from features that require an API key or paid external service.
7. YouTube, Instagram and Facebook
Provide editable channel/profile links at the top of the dashboard.
Allow the user to save their own YouTube, Instagram and Facebook URLs.
Add export-ready settings for each platform.
Add publishing workflow integration only through supported official APIs and authorized user accounts. If publishing is not connected, provide a clear manual export and upload workflow. Do not promise direct publishing without the necessary API permissions.
8. Projects and File Storage
- Create, rename, duplicate, open and delete projects.
- Save project metadata and editable timeline information.
- Allow the user to reopen projects and continue editing.
- Store imported media references and exported video records.
- Provide configurable local storage and download/export options.
- Warn users before deleting media required by a project.
- Add backup and restore for project data.
- Do not store large video files inside localStorage.
