9. Export System
Provide export settings for:
- MP4 where supported.
- Resolution and aspect ratio.
- Frame rate and quality/bitrate.
- Audio inclusion and volume.
- Export progress, cancellation and error handling.
- Download completed videos.
- Save thumbnails and project files separately.
Use a real rendering pipeline. Do not generate a fake download link or report a successful export when rendering has failed. If full MP4 encoding is unsupported, explain the limitation and offer a suitable alternative.
10. Technical Architecture
Use a maintainable component-based frontend, TypeScript and a suitable modern framework such as React.
Use Web Workers where appropriate to keep the interface responsive.
Use a suitable video rendering engine and WebAssembly processing where feasible.
Keep API keys on a secure backend; never expose secret API keys in frontend code.
Use a backend only where needed for authentication, cloud storage, AI integrations or server-side rendering.
Include configuration files, dependency installation instructions and environment variable examples.
11. Security and Reliability
Validate uploaded file types and file sizes. Handle corrupt files, unsupported codecs, insufficient memory and interrupted exports. Ask for confirmation before deleting projects. Keep personal media private and do not upload it to external services without user consent.
12. Required Deliverables
Generate the complete project structure and working source code. Implement the core features first, then add advanced features in stages.
Provide:
1. Project folder structure.
2. Complete source files.
3. Setup and installation commands.
4. Local development and launch instructions.
5. Build and packaging instructions for Windows if supported.
6. A feature test checklist.
7. Clear instructions for configuring optional AI APIs.
8. A list of features that are fully implemented and features that still require integration.
Start by building a working dashboard and one functional editing workflow from media import to preview, timeline editing and export. Test it before proceeding to advanced features. Do not substitute decorative controls for actual functionality.




